<% content_for :title, "About — SceneCore" %>

<section class="px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-16 max-w-6xl mx-auto">
  <div class="max-w-3xl">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-neutral-500 mb-3">About SceneCore</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mb-5">
      Your band. Your fans. Your home.
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-neutral-300 max-w-2xl">
      SceneCore is the music-first digital home where independent bands turn
      discovery into a lasting relationship — through music, content,
      memberships, community, merchandise and events.
    </p>
  </div>

  <nav class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-8 mb-16" aria-label="About this page">
    <% [
         [ "How it works", "#how-it-works" ],
         [ "What it does", "#what-it-does" ],
         [ "Business model", "#business-model" ],
         [ "Technology", "#technology" ],
         [ "Current scope", "#current-scope" ]
       ].each do |label, anchor| %>
      <%= link_to label, anchor, class: "rounded-full border border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-900/60 px-4 py-2 text-sm text-neutral-300 hover:text-white hover:border-neutral-600 transition" %>
    <% end %>
  </nav>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-16">
    <%= render layout: "info_card" do %>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">The fragmented journey</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-300">
        A band is discovered on one service, publishes on another, sells
        somewhere else, and talks to its fans through two or three more.
      </p>
    <% end %>

    <%= render layout: "info_card", locals: { highlighted: true } do %>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">One continuous home</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-300">
        SceneCore keeps the relationship together. The music establishes the
        band's identity; everything else helps that relationship grow.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <section id="how-it-works" class="scroll-mt-28 mb-20">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-yellow-300 mb-3">The product loop</p>
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mb-3">How SceneCore works</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-400 max-w-2xl mb-8">
      Discovery can happen anywhere. SceneCore begins when a listener wants to
      stay connected and support the band directly.
    </p>

    <ol class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-x-10 gap-y-8">
      <% [
           [ "01", "A band builds its home", "It creates a public profile, brings in its music, introduces its members and publishes what is happening now." ],
           [ "02", "A listener becomes a follower", "Visitors can discover and understand a band before creating an account. Following is free when they want to stay." ],
           [ "03", "Membership deepens access", "Fan, Supporter and Core Member unlock progressively closer access for one specific band." ],
           [ "04", "Community keeps the relationship active", "Posts, comments, polls, sessions, credits and direct messages create reasons to return between releases." ],
           [ "05", "Commerce turns support into income", "Fans can buy merchandise, subscribe monthly and purchase tickets without leaving the band's experience." ],
           [ "06", "The band runs it from one panel", "Band administrators manage content, products, orders, events, tickets, members and Stripe payouts." ]
         ].each do |number, title, description| %>
        <li class="flex gap-4">
          <span class="shrink-0 h-9 w-9 rounded-full border border-yellow-500/30 bg-yellow-400/10 text-yellow-300 text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center"><%= number %></span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-white mb-1"><%= title %></h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-neutral-400"><%= description %></p>
          </div>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section id="what-it-does" class="scroll-mt-28 mb-20">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-yellow-300 mb-3">The platform today</p>
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mb-3">What SceneCore does</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-400 max-w-2xl mb-8">
      The product is a multi-band platform. Every band's private data,
      membership access, commerce and administration remain isolated from
      every other band.
    </p>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-5">
      <% [
           [ "Music and discovery", "Public band pages, album publishing, Spotify metadata import, Bandcamp links, covers, ratings and credits." ],
           [ "Memberships", "Monthly Fan, Supporter and Core Member plans with hierarchical access and Stripe-powered lifecycle management." ],
           [ "Exclusive content", "Announcements, demos, alternative versions, rehearsal recordings, composition journals, videos, streams and rare archives." ],
           [ "Community", "Comments, membership polls, voting, private sessions, RSVP and Core Member conversations with the band." ],
           [ "Store", "Products, variants, stock, shipping zones, single-band carts, Stripe Connect checkout, fulfilment and full refunds." ],
           [ "Member benefits", "Merchandise discounts, early product access and priority access enforced by the server, not only hidden in the interface." ],
           [ "Events and tickets", "Published events, free or paid ticket batches, protected reservations, ticket wallet, QR codes and one-time check-in." ],
           [ "Band operations", "Members, content, catalogue, orders, events, tickets, connected Stripe account, balances and upcoming payouts." ],
           [ "Platform governance", "Band approval, moderation, reports, users, subscriptions, categories, fees, analytics, settings and audit history." ]
         ].each do |title, description| %>
        <%= render layout: "info_card" do %>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-white"><%= title %></h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-300"><%= description %></p>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-20">
    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-end sm:justify-between gap-4 mb-8">
      <div>
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-yellow-300 mb-3">Membership</p>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">Three ways to get closer</h2>
      </div>
      <%= link_to "See every benefit", "#{how_it_works_path}#membership-plans", class: "text-sm text-yellow-300 hover:text-yellow-200 transition" %>
    </div>

    <% membership_summaries = {
         "fan" => [ "Follow more closely", "Exclusive posts, early news, selected demos, polls and community access." ],
         "supporter" => [ "Support the creative process", "Everything in Fan, plus early releases, full demos, journals, credits and merchandise benefits." ],
         "core_member" => [ "Join the core group", "Everything in Supporter, plus private sessions, rare archives, direct messages and a voice in selected decisions." ]
       } %>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      <% membership_summaries.each do |level, (promise, description)| %>
        <%= render layout: "info_card", locals: { highlighted: level == "supporter" } do %>
          <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-neutral-500 mb-2"><%= promise %></p>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white"><%= level.humanize.titleize %></h3>
            <p class="mt-2">
              <span class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-white">$<%= Membership::PRICES_IN_CENTS.fetch(level) / 100 %></span>
              <span class="text-sm text-neutral-500">/month</span>
            </p>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-300"><%= description %></p>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-neutral-500 mt-5">
      Membership belongs to one band. A person can be a Fan of one band and a
      Core Member of another. Higher levels inherit the access of lower levels.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="business-model" class="scroll-mt-28 mb-20">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-yellow-300 mb-3">Business model</p>
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mb-3">SceneCore earns when bands earn</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-400 max-w-2xl mb-8">
      There is no monthly platform fee to create a band page. Stripe processes
      payments and separates SceneCore's fee from the band's share at the time
      of the transaction.
    </p>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-5 mb-6">
      <%= render layout: "info_card" do %>
        <p class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-white">85%</p>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">Bands keep 85% of memberships</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-neutral-400">The standard SceneCore share is 15% of recurring membership payments.</p>
      <% end %>

      <%= render layout: "info_card" do %>
        <p class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-white">90%</p>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">Bands keep 90% of store sales</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-neutral-400">The standard SceneCore share is 10% of one-time Store transactions.</p>
      <% end %>

      <%= render layout: "info_card" do %>
        <p class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-white">90%</p>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">Bands keep 90% of paid tickets</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-neutral-400">Paid tickets use the same standard one-time commerce fee as the Store.</p>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-3xl border border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-900/40 p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-white mb-4">Payment flow</h3>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 text-sm">
        <% [
             [ "1", "Band connects Stripe" ],
             [ "2", "Fan checks out" ],
             [ "3", "Stripe separates the fee" ],
             [ "4", "Signed webhooks confirm access" ]
           ].each do |number, label| %>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="shrink-0 h-7 w-7 rounded-full bg-neutral-800 text-neutral-300 font-semibold flex items-center justify-center"><%= number %></span>
            <span class="text-neutral-300"><%= label %></span>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="technology" class="scroll-mt-28 mb-20">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-yellow-300 mb-3">Technology and delivery</p>
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mb-3">A Rails monolith built for a focused MVP</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-400 max-w-2xl mb-8">
      SceneCore deliberately keeps the architecture compact: one application,
      clear domain boundaries and PostgreSQL as the source of truth.
    </p>

    <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-neutral-800 divide-y divide-neutral-800">
      <% [
           [ "Application", "Ruby 3.3 and Rails 8.1, served by Puma and Thruster in a non-root Docker container." ],
           [ "Web interface", "Server-rendered HTML with Hotwire, Turbo, Stimulus, Tailwind CSS, Importmap and Propshaft." ],
           [ "Data and files", "PostgreSQL 16 for transactional data and Active Storage with image processing for media." ],
           [ "Payments", "Stripe Checkout and Stripe Connect for memberships, Store orders, paid tickets, refunds, balances and payouts." ],
           [ "Integrations", "Spotify and Discogs metadata, Bandcamp links, Google Analytics, Sentry monitoring and transactional email." ],
           [ "Deployment", "A multi-stage Docker image deployed on Railway with HTTPS, health checks, database migrations and persistent storage." ],
           [ "CI/CD", "GitHub Actions runs dependency and security scans, RSpec, browser system tests and RuboCop before changes reach main." ],
           [ "Safety", "Devise authentication, Pundit authorization, signed idempotent webhooks, protected files, SSRF controls and atomic stock/check-in rules." ]
         ].each do |label, description| %>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-[11rem_1fr] gap-2 sm:gap-6 px-6 py-5 bg-neutral-900/30">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-white"><%= label %></h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-400"><%= description %></p>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-20">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-yellow-300 mb-3">Clear positioning</p>
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mb-3">What SceneCore is not</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-400 max-w-2xl mb-8">
      Being clear about this is more useful than claiming to replace everything.
    </p>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-5">
      <%= render layout: "info_card" do %>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">Not a streaming replacement</h3>
        <p class="text-neutral-300 text-sm">
          Streaming services remain useful for discovery. SceneCore links out
          to them and becomes the place where that discovery turns into a
          direct relationship.
        </p>
      <% end %>

      <%= render layout: "info_card" do %>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">Not a store with extra features</h3>
        <p class="text-neutral-300 text-sm">
          A purchase is one moment in a relationship. Commerce belongs beside
          the music, content, membership and event that gave the purchase
          meaning.
        </p>
      <% end %>

      <%= render layout: "info_card" do %>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">Not a generic social network</h3>
        <p class="text-neutral-300 text-sm">
          The primary unit is a band's home and its own audience — not a global
          algorithm deciding which band or fan should win attention.
        </p>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="current-scope" class="scroll-mt-28 mb-20">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-yellow-300 mb-3">Current scope</p>
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mb-3">What is live — and what comes next</h2>
    <p class="text-neutral-400 max-w-2xl mb-8">
      The marketplace core is live. The next work is about deeper ticket
      benefits and making the production operation ready for greater scale.
    </p>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <%= render layout: "info_card", locals: { highlighted: true } do %>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">Live now</h3>
        <ul class="flex flex-col gap-2 text-sm text-neutral-300">
          <li>Band pages, music, following and public discovery</li>
          <li>Memberships, exclusive content and community</li>
          <li>Store, discounts, early access and order refunds</li>
          <li>Stripe Connect financial panel</li>
          <li>Native events, paid/free tickets, QR and check-in</li>
          <li>Band and platform administration</li>
        </ul>
      <% end %>

      <%= render layout: "info_card" do %>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">Next increments</h3>
        <ul class="flex flex-col gap-2 text-sm text-neutral-300">
          <li>Membership discounts and priority access for tickets</li>
          <li>Guest ticket checkout and a dedicated door-staff role</li>
          <li>Ticket transfer, automated refunds and camera scanning</li>
          <li>A staging environment and a documented rollback path</li>
          <li>Durable background jobs and shared storage before horizontal scaling</li>
        </ul>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="rounded-3xl border border-yellow-500/30 bg-yellow-400/10 p-6 sm:p-8 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-6">
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Start with the music. Stay for the relationship.</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-300 text-sm max-w-xl">
        Browse independent bands, follow the ones that matter to you, or create
        the digital home your own band can keep building on.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 shrink-0">
      <%= link_to "Discover bands", discover_bands_path, class: "rounded-full bg-yellow-400 text-black font-semibold px-6 py-3 hover:bg-yellow-300 transition" %>
      <% unless user_signed_in? %>
        <%= link_to "Create an account", new_user_registration_path, class: "rounded-full border border-neutral-600 text-white font-semibold px-6 py-3 hover:border-neutral-400 transition" %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
